{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ADy9ibNfupbPZEbpTpKPH9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Regression-based GATE estimator under network interference (starter candidate).\n2\t\n3\tInterface: ``python_rpc_v1:handle``.  ``handle(request) -> response`` takes and returns\n4\tfinite JSON-compatible values only.  The candidate owns all of its state in memory; it\n5\tshares no filesystem with the evaluator and must not read or write evaluator paths.\n6\t\n7\tOperations\n8\t----------\n9\t``{\"op\": \"reset\", \"seed\": <int >= 0>}``\n10\t    Clears ALL candidate state and seeds the candidate RNG.  The seed only initializes\n11\t    randomness; it never identifies a plane, case or workload.  Any non-negative integer\n12\t    is valid.  Response: exactly ``{\"ok\": true}`` (no other keys).\n13\t\n14\t``{\"op\": \"estimate\", ...}``\n15\t    One full dataset from one randomized experiment on a network.  The evaluator sends\n16\t    exactly one ``reset`` per episode and then four ``estimate`` requests in an\n17\t    evaluator-private order.  All four have the identical format and size and the same\n18\t    budget; the candidate must treat every request as an ordinary dataset and must not\n19\t    try to detect which one is which.  Each ``estimate`` is independent: return the best\n20\t    estimate for the request in hand.\n21\t\n22\t    Request fields (all present, no others):\n23\t      op         \"estimate\"\n24\t      n          int, number of nodes (nodes are 0..n-1)\n25\t      edges      array object, undirected unique edges (u < v), dtype int32, shape [E, 2]\n26\t      covariates array object, node covariates, dtype float64, shape [n, 2]\n27\t      treatment  array object, realized treatment assignment, dtype uint8 (0/1), shape [n]\n28\t      outcomes   array object, observed outcomes, dtype float64, shape [n]\n29\t      design     {\"kind\": \"bernoulli\" | \"cluster\",\n30\t                  \"probability\": float,   # marginal treatment probability of the design\n31\t                  \"cluster_labels\": array object (int32, shape [n]) or null}\n32\t                 \"bernoulli\": each node treated independently with ``probability``.\n33\t                 \"cluster\":   whole clusters (``cluster_labels``) are treated together;\n34\t                              exactly round(K*probability) of the K clusters are treated,\n35\t                              chosen uniformly at random.\n36\t      workload   {\"max_op_seconds\": float,  # soft per-request time budget (hard cap is a\n37\t                                            # little larger; exceeding it fails the episode)\n38\t                  \"ci_level\": float}        # nominal level of the requested interval\n39\t\n40\t    Array objects are ``{\"dtype\": \"<name>\", \"shape\": [...], \"encoding\": \"base64-le\",\n41\t    \"data\": \"<base64 of the C-order little-endian buffer>\"}``; see ``decode_array``.\n42\t\n43\t    Target: the global average treatment effect (GATE), i.e. the mean over nodes of\n44\t    Y_i(all nodes treated) - Y_i(all nodes control) for the (hidden) potential outcomes.\n45\t    The interference mechanism, its parameters and the true GATE are never revealed.\n46\t\n47\t    Response (JSON object): required keys ``estimate``, ``ci_low``, ``ci_high``\n48\t    (finite numbers with ci_low <= estimate <= ci_high); optional key ``diagnostics``\n49\t    (a JSON object, at most 4096 bytes serialized; ignored for scoring).  Any other key,\n50\t    a non-finite number, a malformed type or an interval that does not contain the\n51\t    estimate makes that request invalid (the episode keeps its worst-case contribution).\n52\t\n53\tLimits (enforced by the evaluator; a violation is a failed request, never retried):\n54\t  * ``reset`` must answer within 4 s (it includes process/import start-up);\n55\t  * each ``estimate`` must answer within 3 s wall clock (``workload.max_op_seconds`` = 2.5 s\n56\t    is the soft budget to aim for); at most 4 threads of CPU are available;\n57\t  * a complete request is below 0.5 MiB and a complete response must stay far below the\n58\t    64 MiB wire limit (a valid response is < 5 KiB);\n59\t  * no filesystem or network is shared with the evaluator; do not read or write evaluator paths.\n60\tDeterminism: all candidate randomness must derive from the ``reset`` seed, because the evaluator\n61\treplays one episode after a fresh ``reset`` and requires the primary estimate to agree to 1e-6\n62\t(relative to max(1, |estimate|)).\n63\t\n64\tScoring (evaluator-owned): per episode relative error min(|estimate - GATE| / |GATE|, 2),\n65\ta failed/invalid request counts as 2 (and as \"not covered\" with worst-case width);\n66\tRMSE over seeds per case, mean over the 8 cases, ``combined_score`` = -that mean.\n67\tThe evaluator additionally runs matched negative controls (permuted outcomes, node-relabelled\n68\tgraph, constant outcome) through the same operation; a constant-outcome request must\n69\treturn an estimate within 1e-4 of 0, and the run must be deterministic given the reset seed.\n70\t\"\"\"\n71\t\n72\timport base64\n73\t\n74\timport numpy as np\n75\timport scipy.sparse as sp\n76\t\n77\t_STATE = {\"rng\": None, \"seed\": None}\n78\t\n79\t_DTYPES = {\"int32\": \"<i4\", \"float64\": \"<f8\", \"uint8\": \"u1\"}\n80\t\n81\t\n82\tdef decode_array(obj):\n83\t    \"\"\"Decode an array object (see module docstring) into a numpy array.\"\"\"\n84\t    if obj is None:\n85\t        return None\n86\t    if obj[\"encoding\"] != \"base64-le\" or obj[\"dtype\"] not in _DTYPES:\n87\t        raise ValueError(\"unsupported array encoding\")\n88\t    buf = base64.b64decode(obj[\"data\"])\n89\t    return np.frombuffer(buf, dtype=np.dtype(_DTYPES[obj[\"dtype\"]])).reshape(obj[\"shape\"]).copy()\n90\t\n91\t\n92\tdef _adjacency(n, edges):\n93\t    if len(edges) == 0:\n94\t        return sp.csr_matrix((n, n))\n95\t    u, v = edges[:, 0], edges[:, 1]\n96\t    rows = np.concatenate([u, v])\n97\t    cols = np.concatenate([v, u])\n98\t    return sp.csr_matrix((np.ones(len(rows)), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n))\n99\t\n100\t\n101\tdef _features(adj, deg, z, x, treated_all):\n102\t    \"\"\"Design matrix [1, own treatment, neighbour-treated fraction, covariates].\"\"\"\n103\t    if treated_all is None:\n104\t        frac = (adj @ z) / np.maximum(deg, 1.0)\n105\t        own = z\n106\t    else:\n107\t        frac = np.where(deg > 0, float(treated_all), 0.0)\n108\t        own = np.full(len(z), float(treated_all))\n109\t    return np.column_stack([np.ones(len(z)), own, frac, x])\n110\t\n111\t\n112\tdef _parse(request):\n113\t    n = int(request[\"n\"])\n114\t    edges = decode_array(request[\"edges\"])\n115\t    x = decode_array(request[\"covariates\"])\n116\t    z = decode_array(request[\"treatment\"]).astype(np.float64)\n117\t    y = decode_array(request[\"outcomes\"])\n118\t    adj = _adjacency(n, edges)\n119\t    deg = np.asarray(adj.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n120\t    return n, x, z, y, adj, deg\n121\t\n122\t\n123\tZCRIT = 1.959963984540054  # normal quantile for ci_level = 0.95 (the only level requested)\n124\t\n125\t\n126\tdef _exposure_states(adj, deg, z):\n127\t    \"\"\"Exposure summaries for the observed, all-treated and all-control worlds.\n128\t\n129\t    Two-hop quantities use repeated sparse matrix-vector products only (never adj @ adj).\n130\t    \"\"\"\n131\t    n = len(z)\n132\t    ones = np.ones(n)\n133\t    walks2 = adj @ (adj @ ones)  # number of length-2 walks starting at each node\n134\t    s1 = adj @ z\n135\t    obs = {\n136\t        \"own\": z,\n137\t        \"s1\": s1,\n138\t        \"f1\": s1 / np.maximum(deg, 1.0),\n139\t        \"f2\": (adj @ (adj @ z)) / np.maximum(walks2, 1.0),\n140\t    }\n141\t    all1 = {\n142\t        \"own\": ones,\n143\t        \"s1\": deg.astype(np.float64),\n144\t        \"f1\": (deg > 0).astype(np.float64),\n145\t        \"f2\": (walks2 > 0).astype(np.float64),\n146\t    }\n147\t    all0 = {\"own\": np.zeros(n), \"s1\": np.zeros(n), \"f1\": np.zeros(n), \"f2\": np.zeros(n)}\n148\t    return obs, all1, all0\n149\t\n150\t\n151\tdef candidate_designs(deg, x):\n152\t    \"\"\"Library of few-parameter exposure mappings.\n153\t\n154\t    Returns {name: (builder, count_cols)}; builder(state) -> design matrix with columns\n155\t    [1, own, exposure features..., (x or interactions)].  ``count_cols`` marks columns that\n156\t    are unbounded treated-neighbour counts (all-treated values get winsorised).\n157\t    \"\"\"\n158\t    n = len(deg)\n159\t    pos = deg[deg > 0]\n160\t    median_deg = max(float(np.median(pos)), 1.0) if len(pos) else 1.0\n161\t    mean_deg = max(float(np.mean(deg)), 1.0)\n162\t    ld = np.log1p(deg)\n163\t    ldc = ld - ld.mean()\n164\t    xc = x - x.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n165\t    one = np.ones(n)\n166\t\n167\t    def lin(s):\n168\t        return np.column_stack([one, s[\"own\"], s[\"f1\"], x])\n169\t\n170\t    specs = {\"M0_linear\": (lin, ())}\n171\t\n172\t    specs[\"M1_count\"] = (\n173\t        lambda s: np.column_stack([one, s[\"own\"], s[\"s1\"] / mean_deg, x]),\n174\t        (2,),\n175\t    )\n176\t    specs[\"M2_twohop\"] = (\n177\t        lambda s: np.column_stack([one, s[\"own\"], s[\"f1\"], s[\"f2\"], x]),\n178\t        (),\n179\t    )\n180\t    specs[\"M3_interact\"] = (\n181\t        lambda s: np.column_stack(\n182\t            [one, s[\"own\"], s[\"f1\"], x, ldc, s[\"own\"] * ldc, s[\"own\"] * xc,\n183\t             s[\"f1\"] * ldc]\n184\t        ),\n185\t        (),\n186\t    )\n187\t    specs[\"M3b_own_deg_frac_deg\"] = (\n188\t        lambda s: np.column_stack(\n189\t            [one, s[\"own\"], s[\"f1\"], x, ldc, s[\"own\"] * ldc, s[\"f1\"] * ldc]\n190\t        ),\n191\t        (),\n192\t    )\n193\t    specs[\"M3c_frac_x\"] = (\n194\t        lambda s: np.column_stack([one, s[\"own\"], s[\"f1\"], x, s[\"f1\"] * xc]),\n195\t        (),\n196\t    )\n197\t    for k in (1.0, 3.0, 8.0):\n198\t        specs[\"M4_sat_k%g\" % k] = (\n199\t            (lambda s, k=k: np.column_stack([one, s[\"own\"], 1.0 - np.exp(-k * s[\"f1\"]), x])),\n200\t            (),\n201\t        )\n202\t    for t in (0.25, 0.5, 0.75):\n203\t        specs[\"M5_sig_t%g\" % t] = (\n204\t            (lambda s, t=t: np.column_stack(\n205\t                [one, s[\"own\"], 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-(s[\"f1\"] - t) / 0.1)), x])),\n206\t            (),\n207\t        )\n208\t    for k in (0.5, 1.0, 2.0):\n209\t        specs[\"M6_satcount_k%g\" % k] = (\n210\t            (lambda s, k=k: np.column_stack(\n211\t                [one, s[\"own\"], 1.0 - np.exp(-s[\"s1\"] / (k * median_deg)), x])),\n212\t            (),\n213\t        )\n214\t    return specs\n215\t\n216\t\n217\tdef sandwich_se(x_obs, resid, contrast, n):\n218\t    \"\"\"HC1 sandwich delta-method standard error of contrast @ beta.\"\"\"\n219\t    bread = np.linalg.pinv(x_obs.T @ x_obs)\n220\t    meat = (x_obs * resid[:, None] ** 2).T @ x_obs\n221\t    cov = bread @ meat @ bread * n / max(n - x_obs.shape[1], 1)\n222\t    return float(np.sqrt(max(contrast @ cov @ contrast, 0.0)))\n223\t\n224\t\n225\tdef _fit_candidate(builder, count_cols, states, y):\n226\t    obs, all1, all0 = states\n227\t    n = len(y)\n228\t    x_obs = builder(obs)\n229\t    x1 = builder(all1)\n230\t    x0 = builder(all0)\n231\t    for c in count_cols:  # winsorise count-type all-treated features\n232\t        cap = 3.0 * float(np.percentile(x_obs[:, c], 99.5))\n233\t        if cap > 0:\n234\t            x1[:, c] = np.minimum(x1[:, c], cap)\n235\t    if not (np.all(np.isfinite(x_obs)) and np.all(np.isfinite(x1)) and np.all(np.isfinite(x0))):\n236\t        return None\n237\t    beta, _, rank, _ = np.linalg.lstsq(x_obs, y, rcond=None)\n238\t    resid = y - x_obs @ beta\n239\t    rss = float(resid @ resid)\n240\t    contrast = (x1 - x0).mean(axis=0)\n241\t    est = float(contrast @ beta)\n242\t    se = sandwich_se(x_obs, resid, contrast, n)\n243\t    if not (np.isfinite(est) and np.isfinite(se)):\n244\t        return None\n245\t    return {\"est\": est, \"se\": se, \"rss\": rss, \"p\": int(rank)}\n246\t\n247\t\n248\tdef bic_gate(fits, n, y_var, bic_margin=10.0):\n249\t    \"\"\"Keep the linear fit unless a candidate beats it by BIC > bic_margin.\n250\t\n251\t    Passing candidates are averaged with BIC weights.  Returns (est, se, est0, se0).\n252\t    \"\"\"\n253\t    base = fits[\"M0_linear\"]\n254\t    est0, se0 = base[\"est\"], base[\"se\"]\n255\t    floor = 1e-12 * y_var\n256\t\n257\t    def bic(f):\n258\t        return n * np.log(np.maximum(f[\"rss\"] / n, floor)) + f[\"p\"] * np.log(n)\n259\t\n260\t    bic0 = bic(base)\n261\t    passing = []\n262\t    for name, f in fits.items():\n263\t        if name == \"M0_linear\" or f is None:\n264\t            continue\n265\t        b = bic(f)\n266\t        if bic0 - b > bic_margin:\n267\t            passing.append((b, f))\n268\t    if not passing:\n269\t        return est0, se0, est0, se0\n270\t    bmin = min(b for b, _ in passing)\n271\t    w = np.array([np.exp(-0.5 * (b - bmin)) for b, _ in passing])\n272\t    w = w / w.sum()\n273\t    ests = np.array([f[\"est\"] for _, f in passing])\n274\t    ses = np.array([f[\"se\"] for _, f in passing])\n275\t    est = float(w @ ests)\n276\t    spread = float(np.sqrt(w @ (ests - est) ** 2))\n277\t    se = float(w @ ses) + spread\n278\t    # sanity guard: do not stray far from the linear estimate\n279\t    if abs(est - est0) > 3.0 * max(abs(est0), se0) or not (np.isfinite(est) and np.isfinite(se)):\n280\t        return est0, se0, est0, se0\n281\t    return est, se, est0, se0\n282\t\n283\t\n284\tdef _estimate(request):\n285\t    try:\n286\t        n, x, z, y, adj, deg = _parse(request)\n287\t        y_var = float(np.var(y))\n288\t        if y_var == 0.0:\n289\t            return {\"estimate\": 0.0, \"ci_low\": 0.0, \"ci_high\": 0.0}\n290\t        states = _exposure_states(adj, deg, z)\n291\t        fits = {}\n292\t        for name, (builder, count_cols) in candidate_designs(deg, x).items():\n293\t            try:\n294\t                fits[name] = _fit_candidate(builder, count_cols, states, y)\n295\t            except Exception:\n296\t                fits[name] = None\n297\t        if fits.get(\"M0_linear\") is None:\n298\t            raise ValueError(\"linear fit failed\")\n299\t        est, se, est0, se0 = bic_gate(fits, n, y_var, bic_margin=10.0)\n300\t        half = ZCRIT * se + abs(est - est0)\n301\t        if not (np.isfinite(est) and np.isfinite(half)):\n302\t            raise ValueError(\"non-finite\")\n303\t        return {\"estimate\": est, \"ci_low\": est - half, \"ci_high\": est + half}\n304\t    except Exception:\n305\t        return _estimate_linear(request)\n306\t\n307\t\n308\tdef _estimate_linear(request):\n309\t    n, x, z, y, adj, deg = _parse(request)\n310\t\n311\t    x_obs = _features(adj, deg, z, x, None)\n312\t    beta, *_ = np.linalg.lstsq(x_obs, y, rcond=None)\n313\t    resid = y - x_obs @ beta\n314\t    # GATE = mean over nodes of prediction(all treated) - prediction(all control).\n315\t    contrast = (_features(adj, deg, z, x, 1) - _features(adj, deg, z, x, 0)).mean(axis=0)\n316\t    est = float(contrast @ beta)\n317\t\n318\t    # Heteroskedasticity-robust (HC1) sandwich interval for the linear functional.\n319\t    bread = np.linalg.pinv(x_obs.T @ x_obs)\n320\t    meat = (x_obs * resid[:, None] ** 2).T @ x_obs\n321\t    cov = bread @ meat @ bread * n / max(n - x_obs.shape[1], 1)\n322\t    se = float(np.sqrt(max(contrast @ cov @ contrast, 0.0)))\n323\t    zcrit = 1.959963984540054  # normal quantile for ci_level = 0.95 (the only level requested)\n324\t    return {\"estimate\": est, \"ci_low\": est - zcrit * se, \"ci_high\": est + zcrit * se}\n325\t\n326\t\n327\tdef handle(request):\n328\t    op = request.get(\"op\")\n329\t    if op == \"reset\":\n330\t        seed = int(request[\"seed\"])\n331\t        _STATE[\"seed\"] = seed\n332\t        _STATE[\"rng\"] = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n333\t        return {\"ok\": True}\n334\t    if op == \"estimate\":\n335\t        return _estimate(request)\n336\t    raise ValueError(\"unknown op\")\n337\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c5763a6a-5113-409b-b2f9-b2a46f5c58bf","uuid":"81a105d2-59e6-4156-acbc-5853330c6a9a","timestamp":"2026-11-11T09:00:35.474Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/source_evidence/frozen_estimator/program.py","content":"\"\"\"Regression-based GATE estimator under network interference (starter candidate).\n\nInterface: ``python_rpc_v1:handle``.  ``handle(request) -> response`` takes and returns\nfinite JSON-compatible values only.  The candidate owns all of its state in memory; it\nshares no filesystem with the evaluator and must not read or write evaluator paths.\n\nOperations\n----------\n``{\"op\": \"reset\", \"seed\": <int >= 0>}``\n    Clears ALL candidate state and seeds the candidate RNG.  The seed only initializes\n    randomness; it never identifies a plane, case or workload.  Any non-negative integer\n    is valid.  Response: exactly ``{\"ok\": true}`` (no other keys).\n\n``{\"op\": \"estimate\", ...}``\n    One full dataset from one randomized experiment on a network.  The evaluator sends\n    exactly one ``reset`` per episode and then four ``estimate`` requests in an\n    evaluator-private order.  All four have the identical format and size and the same\n    budget; the candidate must treat every request as an ordinary dataset and must not\n    try to detect which one is which.  Each ``estimate`` is independent: return the best\n    estimate for the request in hand.\n\n    Request fields (all present, no others):\n      op         \"estimate\"\n      n          int, number of nodes (nodes are 0..n-1)\n      edges      array object, undirected unique edges (u < v), dtype int32, shape [E, 2]\n      covariates array object, node covariates, dtype float64, shape [n, 2]\n      treatment  array object, realized treatment assignment, dtype uint8 (0/1), shape [n]\n      outcomes   array object, observed outcomes, dtype float64, shape [n]\n      design     {\"kind\": \"bernoulli\" | \"cluster\",\n                  \"probability\": float,   # marginal treatment probability of the design\n                  \"cluster_labels\": array object (int32, shape [n]) or null}\n                 \"bernoulli\": each node treated independently with ``probability``.\n                 \"cluster\":   whole clusters (``cluster_labels``) are treated together;\n                              exactly round(K*probability) of the K clusters are treated,\n                              chosen uniformly at random.\n      workload   {\"max_op_seconds\": float,  # soft per-request time budget (hard cap is a\n                                            # little larger; exceeding it fails the episode)\n                  \"ci_level\": float}        # nominal level of the requested interval\n\n    Array objects are ``{\"dtype\": \"<name>\", \"shape\": [...], \"encoding\": \"base64-le\",\n    \"data\": \"<base64 of the C-order little-endian buffer>\"}``; see ``decode_array``.\n\n    Target: the global average treatment effect (GATE), i.e. the mean over nodes of\n    Y_i(all nodes treated) - Y_i(all nodes control) for the (hidden) potential outcomes.\n    The interference mechanism, its parameters and the true GATE are never revealed.\n\n    Response (JSON object): required keys ``estimate``, ``ci_low``, ``ci_high``\n    (finite numbers with ci_low <= estimate <= ci_high); optional key ``diagnostics``\n    (a JSON object, at most 4096 bytes serialized; ignored for scoring).  Any other key,\n    a non-finite number, a malformed type or an interval that does not contain the\n    estimate makes that request invalid (the episode keeps its worst-case contribution).\n\nLimits (enforced by the evaluator; a violation is a failed request, never retried):\n  * ``reset`` must answer within 4 s (it includes process/import start-up);\n  * each ``estimate`` must answer within 3 s wall clock (``workload.max_op_seconds`` = 2.5 s\n    is the soft budget to aim for); at most 4 threads of CPU are available;\n  * a complete request is below 0.5 MiB and a complete response must stay far below the\n    64 MiB wire limit (a valid response is < 5 KiB);\n  * no filesystem or network is shared with the evaluator; do not read or write evaluator paths.\nDeterminism: all candidate randomness must derive from the ``reset`` seed, because the evaluator\nreplays one episode after a fresh ``reset`` and requires the primary estimate to agree to 1e-6\n(relative to max(1, |estimate|)).\n\nScoring (evaluator-owned): per episode relative error min(|estimate - GATE| / |GATE|, 2),\na failed/invalid request counts as 2 (and as \"not covered\" with worst-case width);\nRMSE over seeds per case, mean over the 8 cases, ``combined_score`` = -that mean.\nThe evaluator additionally runs matched negative controls (permuted outcomes, node-relabelled\ngraph, constant outcome) through the same operation; a constant-outcome request must\nreturn an estimate within 1e-4 of 0, and the run must be deterministic given the reset seed.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport base64\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\n\n_STATE = {\"rng\": None, \"seed\": None}\n\n_DTYPES = {\"int32\": \"<i4\", \"float64\": \"<f8\", \"uint8\": \"u1\"}\n\n\ndef decode_array(obj):\n    \"\"\"Decode an array object (see module docstring) into a numpy array.\"\"\"\n    if obj is None:\n        return None\n    if obj[\"encoding\"] != \"base64-le\" or obj[\"dtype\"] not in _DTYPES:\n        raise ValueError(\"unsupported array encoding\")\n    buf = base64.b64decode(obj[\"data\"])\n    return np.frombuffer(buf, dtype=np.dtype(_DTYPES[obj[\"dtype\"]])).reshape(obj[\"shape\"]).copy()\n\n\ndef _adjacency(n, edges):\n    if len(edges) == 0:\n        return sp.csr_matrix((n, n))\n    u, v = edges[:, 0], edges[:, 1]\n    rows = np.concatenate([u, v])\n    cols = np.concatenate([v, u])\n    return sp.csr_matrix((np.ones(len(rows)), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n))\n\n\ndef _features(adj, deg, z, x, treated_all):\n    \"\"\"Design matrix [1, own treatment, neighbour-treated fraction, covariates].\"\"\"\n    if treated_all is None:\n        frac = (adj @ z) / np.maximum(deg, 1.0)\n        own = z\n    else:\n        frac = np.where(deg > 0, float(treated_all), 0.0)\n        own = np.full(len(z), float(treated_all))\n    return np.column_stack([np.ones(len(z)), own, frac, x])\n\n\ndef _parse(request):\n    n = int(request[\"n\"])\n    edges = decode_array(request[\"edges\"])\n    x = decode_array(request[\"covariates\"])\n    z = decode_array(request[\"treatment\"]).astype(np.float64)\n    y = decode_array(request[\"outcomes\"])\n    adj = _adjacency(n, edges)\n    deg = np.asarray(adj.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n    return n, x, z, y, adj, deg\n\n\nZCRIT = 1.959963984540054  # normal quantile for ci_level = 0.95 (the only level requested)\n\n\ndef _exposure_states(adj, deg, z):\n    \"\"\"Exposure summaries for the observed, all-treated and all-control worlds.\n\n    Two-hop quantities use repeated sparse matrix-vector products only (never adj @ adj).\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(z)\n    ones = np.ones(n)\n    walks2 = adj @ (adj @ ones)  # number of length-2 walks starting at each node\n    s1 = adj @ z\n    obs = {\n        \"own\": z,\n        \"s1\": s1,\n        \"f1\": s1 / np.maximum(deg, 1.0),\n        \"f2\": (adj @ (adj @ z)) / np.maximum(walks2, 1.0),\n    }\n    all1 = {\n        \"own\": ones,\n        \"s1\": deg.astype(np.float64),\n        \"f1\": (deg > 0).astype(np.float64),\n        \"f2\": (walks2 > 0).astype(np.float64),\n    }\n    all0 = {\"own\": np.zeros(n), \"s1\": np.zeros(n), \"f1\": np.zeros(n), \"f2\": np.zeros(n)}\n    return obs, all1, all0\n\n\ndef candidate_designs(deg, x):\n    \"\"\"Library of few-parameter exposure mappings.\n\n    Returns {name: (builder, count_cols)}; builder(state) -> design matrix with columns\n    [1, own, exposure features..., (x or interactions)].  ``count_cols`` marks columns that\n    are unbounded treated-neighbour counts (all-treated values get winsorised).\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(deg)\n    pos = deg[deg > 0]\n    median_deg = max(float(np.median(pos)), 1.0) if len(pos) else 1.0\n    mean_deg = max(float(np.mean(deg)), 1.0)\n    ld = np.log1p(deg)\n    ldc = ld - ld.mean()\n    xc = x - x.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    one = np.ones(n)\n\n    def lin(s):\n        return np.column_stack([one, s[\"own\"], s[\"f1\"], x])\n\n    specs = {\"M0_linear\": (lin, ())}\n\n    specs[\"M1_count\"] = (\n        lambda s: np.column_stack([one, s[\"own\"], s[\"s1\"] / mean_deg, x]),\n        (2,),\n    )\n    specs[\"M2_twohop\"] = (\n        lambda s: np.column_stack([one, s[\"own\"], s[\"f1\"], s[\"f2\"], x]),\n        (),\n    )\n    specs[\"M3_interact\"] = (\n        lambda s: np.column_stack(\n            [one, s[\"own\"], s[\"f1\"], x, ldc, s[\"own\"] * ldc, s[\"own\"] * xc,\n             s[\"f1\"] * ldc]\n        ),\n        (),\n    )\n    specs[\"M3b_own_deg_frac_deg\"] = (\n        lambda s: np.column_stack(\n            [one, s[\"own\"], s[\"f1\"], x, ldc, s[\"own\"] * ldc, s[\"f1\"] * ldc]\n        ),\n        (),\n    )\n    specs[\"M3c_frac_x\"] = (\n        lambda s: np.column_stack([one, s[\"own\"], s[\"f1\"], x, s[\"f1\"] * xc]),\n        (),\n    )\n    for k in (1.0, 3.0, 8.0):\n        specs[\"M4_sat_k%g\" % k] = (\n            (lambda s, k=k: np.column_stack([one, s[\"own\"], 1.0 - np.exp(-k * s[\"f1\"]), x])),\n            (),\n        )\n    for t in (0.25, 0.5, 0.75):\n        specs[\"M5_sig_t%g\" % t] = (\n            (lambda s, t=t: np.column_stack(\n                [one, s[\"own\"], 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-(s[\"f1\"] - t) / 0.1)), x])),\n            (),\n        )\n    for k in (0.5, 1.0, 2.0):\n        specs[\"M6_satcount_k%g\" % k] = (\n            (lambda s, k=k: np.column_stack(\n                [one, s[\"own\"], 1.0 - np.exp(-s[\"s1\"] / (k * median_deg)), x])),\n            (),\n        )\n    return specs\n\n\ndef sandwich_se(x_obs, resid, contrast, n):\n    \"\"\"HC1 sandwich delta-method standard error of contrast @ beta.\"\"\"\n    bread = np.linalg.pinv(x_obs.T @ x_obs)\n    meat = (x_obs * resid[:, None] ** 2).T @ x_obs\n    cov = bread @ meat @ bread * n / max(n - x_obs.shape[1], 1)\n    return float(np.sqrt(max(contrast @ cov @ contrast, 0.0)))\n\n\ndef _fit_candidate(builder, count_cols, states, y):\n    obs, all1, all0 = states\n    n = len(y)\n    x_obs = builder(obs)\n    x1 = builder(all1)\n    x0 = builder(all0)\n    for c in count_cols:  # winsorise count-type all-treated features\n        cap = 3.0 * float(np.percentile(x_obs[:, c], 99.5))\n        if cap > 0:\n            x1[:, c] = np.minimum(x1[:, c], cap)\n    if not (np.all(np.isfinite(x_obs)) and np.all(np.isfinite(x1)) and np.all(np.isfinite(x0))):\n        return None\n    beta, _, rank, _ = np.linalg.lstsq(x_obs, y, rcond=None)\n    resid = y - x_obs @ beta\n    rss = float(resid @ resid)\n    contrast = (x1 - x0).mean(axis=0)\n    est = float(contrast @ beta)\n    se = sandwich_se(x_obs, resid, contrast, n)\n    if not (np.isfinite(est) and np.isfinite(se)):\n        return None\n    return {\"est\": est, \"se\": se, \"rss\": rss, \"p\": int(rank)}\n\n\ndef bic_gate(fits, n, y_var, bic_margin=10.0):\n    \"\"\"Keep the linear fit unless a candidate beats it by BIC > bic_margin.\n\n    Passing candidates are averaged with BIC weights.  Returns (est, se, est0, se0).\n    \"\"\"\n    base = fits[\"M0_linear\"]\n    est0, se0 = base[\"est\"], base[\"se\"]\n    floor = 1e-12 * y_var\n\n    def bic(f):\n        return n * np.log(np.maximum(f[\"rss\"] / n, floor)) + f[\"p\"] * np.log(n)\n\n    bic0 = bic(base)\n    passing = []\n    for name, f in fits.items():\n        if name == \"M0_linear\" or f is None:\n            continue\n        b = bic(f)\n        if bic0 - b > bic_margin:\n            passing.append((b, f))\n    if not passing:\n        return est0, se0, est0, se0\n    bmin = min(b for b, _ in passing)\n    w = np.array([np.exp(-0.5 * (b - bmin)) for b, _ in passing])\n    w = w / w.sum()\n    ests = np.array([f[\"est\"] for _, f in passing])\n    ses = np.array([f[\"se\"] for _, f in passing])\n    est = float(w @ ests)\n    spread = float(np.sqrt(w @ (ests - est) ** 2))\n    se = float(w @ ses) + spread\n    # sanity guard: do not stray far from the linear estimate\n    if abs(est - est0) > 3.0 * max(abs(est0), se0) or not (np.isfinite(est) and np.isfinite(se)):\n        return est0, se0, est0, se0\n    return est, se, est0, se0\n\n\ndef _estimate(request):\n    try:\n        n, x, z, y, adj, deg = _parse(request)\n        y_var = float(np.var(y))\n        if y_var == 0.0:\n            return {\"estimate\": 0.0, \"ci_low\": 0.0, \"ci_high\": 0.0}\n        states = _exposure_states(adj, deg, z)\n        fits = {}\n        for name, (builder, count_cols) in candidate_designs(deg, x).items():\n            try:\n                fits[name] = _fit_candidate(builder, count_cols, states, y)\n            except Exception:\n                fits[name] = None\n        if fits.get(\"M0_linear\") is None:\n            raise ValueError(\"linear fit failed\")\n        est, se, est0, se0 = bic_gate(fits, n, y_var, bic_margin=10.0)\n        half = ZCRIT * se + abs(est - est0)\n        if not (np.isfinite(est) and np.isfinite(half)):\n            raise ValueError(\"non-finite\")\n        return {\"estimate\": est, \"ci_low\": est - half, \"ci_high\": est + half}\n    except Exception:\n        return _estimate_linear(request)\n\n\ndef _estimate_linear(request):\n    n, x, z, y, adj, deg = _parse(request)\n\n    x_obs = _features(adj, deg, z, x, None)\n    beta, *_ = np.linalg.lstsq(x_obs, y, rcond=None)\n    resid = y - x_obs @ beta\n    # GATE = mean over nodes of prediction(all treated) - prediction(all control).\n    contrast = (_features(adj, deg, z, x, 1) - _features(adj, deg, z, x, 0)).mean(axis=0)\n    est = float(contrast @ beta)\n\n    # Heteroskedasticity-robust (HC1) sandwich interval for the linear functional.\n    bread = np.linalg.pinv(x_obs.T @ x_obs)\n    meat = (x_obs * resid[:, None] ** 2).T @ x_obs\n    cov = bread @ meat @ bread * n / max(n - x_obs.shape[1], 1)\n    se = float(np.sqrt(max(contrast @ cov @ contrast, 0.0)))\n    zcrit = 1.959963984540054  # normal quantile for ci_level = 0.95 (the only level requested)\n    return {\"estimate\": est, \"ci_low\": est - zcrit * se, \"ci_high\": est + zcrit * se}\n\n\ndef handle(request):\n    op = request.get(\"op\")\n    if op == \"reset\":\n        seed = int(request[\"seed\"])\n        _STATE[\"seed\"] = seed\n        _STATE[\"rng\"] = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n        return {\"ok\": True}\n    if op == \"estimate\":\n        return _estimate(request)\n    raise ValueError(\"unknown op\")\n","numLines":337,"startLine":1,"totalLines":337}}}
